 "description": "Returns the standard, reduced, super-reduced and parking VAT rates for a single European country, plus the VAT number format and regex. Read-only and offline: no network call, no API key, no rate limit, no side effects. Accepts ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes (DE, FR, IT, \u2026); also covers non-EU European jurisdictions where available (NO, CH, GB, UA, TR, \u2026). Output: { countryCode, countryName, vatName, vatAbbr, currency, standardRate, reducedRates[], superReducedRate, parkingRate, vatNumberFormat, vatNumberPattern, identifiers, updatedAt }; rates are percentages and may be null where not applicable. `identifiers` holds the names (not numbers) of the company registrar, the company register, the register number, the tax ID and the VAT ID, each keyed by language (every official language plus \"en\") or null, e.g. registryCodeName for FI is { fi: \"Y-tunnus\", sv: \"FO-nummer\", en: \"Business ID\" }. Returns an error if the country code is unknown. Use when the user asks \"what is the VAT rate in X\" or needs the VAT number format for a country. Free, no API key required.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
